.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-flow-export - Print a flow's script, or write every flow to a directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work flow export NAME|--all DIR [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a flow's script on standard output, verbatim, so that a redirection
writes the file an import takes back unchanged.

.PP
--all writes one \&.star per unarchived flow into the directory, which is
created if it is missing, and prints nothing.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	Write every flow into the directory given as the argument

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for export


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
git work flow export board > flows/board.star
git work flow export --all flows/
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-flow(1)\fP
